Lifecycle contract proposed for planner
close is idempotent and terminal for this instance: stop observations/channel; prohibit new DB opens, queued lock callbacks and new work; close both resolved connections and any late success from a pending/rejected open. versionchange and abnormal close retire the instance/cache; a fresh page/store instance must reopen. onblocked rejection marks that particular open abandoned; later upgrade should abort where possible, and later success closes the DB instead of retaining an orphan. Never let an old open's cleanup overwrite a newer generation. Check closed state after awaits before creating transactions/entering callbacks. Do not forcibly release a held identity lock before its operation drains.

An already created transaction must report its real completion/abort; close must not recast a committed durable write as failure or cancel record bookkeeping for an act already sent. Close connection promptly and let existing transactions drain. If write read-back is required after close, allow that bounded in-flight operation's verification without granting a new public operation; close the verifying connection when done. Prevent pending writes from recreating the channel.

BroadcastChannel is optional: catch construction/post failure independently, keep local observer delivery, and do not reject a committed/read-back-verified write. Treat messages only as invalidation hints; consumers reread actual custody. No observer callback owns a write. Do not add polling or grant authority from a message.

